ed unusually large spring volatility, so the interval allows for administrative timing effects","No new COLA step occurs in May, limiting upside versus January-like jumps"],"sourceContext":["https://www.bea.gov/news/schedule","https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-income","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/W823RC1","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/data/W823RC1"],"runAt":"2026-06-17T02:28:12Z","reasoning":[{"kind":"heading","text":"Forecast BEA May 2026 Social Security Benefits"},{"kind":"text","text":"The target is BEA's first-print May 2026 value for Personal current transfer receipts: Government social benefits to persons: Social security, reported in billions of dollars at a seasonally adjusted annual rate."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked the BEA release schedule for Personal Income and Outlays, May 2026.","result":"BEA schedule lists Personal Income and Outlays, May 2026 on June 25, 2026 at 8:30 AM."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked BEA's Personal Income page for the current release status and next release.","result":"BEA Personal Income page shows the current release is May 28, 2026, next release June 25, 2026, and April personal income changed 0.0%."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"history.lookup","call":"Checked FRED's BEA-sourced W823RC1 series page for latest observations and metadata.","result":"Fetched W823RC1 latest values: Apr 2026 1643.7, Mar 2026 1636.9, Feb 2026 1628.6, Jan 2026 1623.2; units are billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted annual rate."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"history.lookup","call":"Checked the FRED table-data view for the longer recent monthly history.","result":"Fetched recent history: 2025-04 1678.6, 2025-05 1556.0, 2025-06 1587.9, 2025-12 1575.3, 2026-01 1623.2, 2026-04 1643.7."},{"kind":"text","text":"Base-rate/reference-class: outside one-time administrative jumps, this series usually moves gradually month to month; recent ordinary May changes include 2023 Apr-May +3.5 and 2024 Apr-May +2.1, while 2025 Apr-May -122.6 was an exceptional unwind from spring volatility."},{"kind":"math","text":"Recent 2026 monthly changes were +5.4 from January to February, +8.3 from February to March, and +6.8 from March to April, averaging about +6.8. Applying +6.8 to Apr 2026 value 1643.7 gives 1650.5. I use an 80% interval of 1638.0 to 1663.0, wide enough for normal first-print noise and smaller administrative timing shifts."},{"kind":"text","text":"Counter-consideration: 2025 showed unusually large Social Security volatility around March to May, so a pure smooth-trend forecast could be too narrow if BEA records another timing or retroactive-payment effect. I still center on smooth growth because 2026 through April shows no comparable spike."},{"kind":"forecast","point":1650.5,"ciLow":1638,"ciHigh":1663}]}
records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-04-41z-abs-labour-employment-change-2026-05/raw_response.txt:1:{"slug":"abs-labour-employment-change-2026-05","country":"AU","type":"data","title":"Australia employment change, May 2026","question":"ABS Labour Force, Australia seasonally adjusted employed people monthly change for May 2026, first print","unit":"thousands","pointEstimate":20,"ciLow":-35,"ciHigh":75,"confidence":0.8,"resolutionDate":"2026-06-25","resolutionSource":"Australian Bureau of Statistics Labour Force, Australia, May 2026 first release","resolutionSourceUrl":"https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/labour/employment-and-unemployment/labour-force-australia/may-2026","resolutionRule":"Resolve to the first-published ABS Labour Force, Australia May 2026 seasonally adjusted monthly change in employed people, expressed in thousands of people. Use the first print on the May 2026 release page and do not revise for later ABS revisions or annual seasonal-adjustment updates. If ABS reports people rather than thousands, divide by 1,000.","dataPointId":"abs.labour.employed_people.seasonally_adjusted.monthly_change.2026-05.first_print","historicalContext":[{"label":"Apr 2026 first-print monthly change, seasonally adjusted, thousands","value":-18.6},{"label":"Mar 2026 implied monthly change from ABS seasonally adjusted levels, thousands","value":23.3},{"label":"Feb 2026 implied monthly change from ABS seasonally adjusted levels, thousands","value":28.9},{"label":"2023-2025 May average implied monthly change, seasonally adjusted, thousands","value":26}],"drivers":["Recent trend employment growth near 20 thousand per month","April seasonally adjusted employment fell 18.6 thousand after February-March gains","May seasonal history is mixed but positive on average across 2023-2025","Unemployment rose to 4.5 percent in April, pointing to softer labour demand","ABS flagged two incoming rotation groups for May, increasing survey-noise risk"],"sourceContext":["https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/labour/employment-and-unemployment/labour-force-australia/latest-release","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/labour/employment-and-unemployment/labour-force-australia","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/labour/employment-and-unemployment/labour-force-australia/apr-2026"],"runAt":"2026-06-17T02:05:03Z","reasoning":[{"kind":"heading","text":"Forecast: ABS May 2026 employment change"},{"kind":"text","text":"The resolver is the first ABS Labour Force, Australia May 2026 release, specifically the seasonally adjusted monthly change in employed people. The unit here is thousands of people, matching the ABS headline convention."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked the ABS Labour Force, Australia all-releases page for the scheduled May 2026 publication date.","result":"ABS lists Labour Force, Australia, May 2026 with release date 25/06/2026 at 11:30am AEST."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Checked the ABS April 2026 latest-release key statistics for the most recent official first-print labour-market state.","result":"ABS reported April 2026 seasonally adjusted employment decreased by 18,600 to 14,737,400 people, unemployment rose by 33,000 to 692,500 people, and the unemployment rate was 4.5%."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Read the ABS employment graph table on the April 2026 release for recent seasonally adjusted employed-people levels.","result":"ABS seasonally adjusted employed people were 14,664.2 thousand in Dec-25, 14,703.8 in Jan-26, 14,732.7 in Feb-26, 14,756.0 in Mar-26, and 14,737.4 in Apr-26."},{"kind":"tool","tool":"official.lookup","call":"Read the same ABS table for prior May observations to form a May reference class.","result":"ABS seasonally adjusted employed people were 13,930.4 thousand in Apr-23 and 14,010.0 in May-23, 14,268.9 in Apr-24 and 14,288.4 in May-24, and 14,608.4 in Apr-25 and 14,587.2 in May-25."},{"kind":"text","text":"Base-rate/reference class: the three most recent May changes were +79.6 thousand, +19.5 thousand, and -21.2 thousand, averaging about +26.0 thousand. Recent non-May momentum before April was also positive, with February and March gains around +28.9 thousand and +23.3 thousand."},{"kind":"math","text":"Recent trend growth from ABS trend levels was +22.1 thousand in April; the 2023-2025 May average was +26.0 thousand; the latest seasonally adjusted print was -18.6 thousand. I weight underlying trend and May base rate more than April noise: about 0.45*22.1 + 0.35*26.0 + 0.20*(-18.6) = 15.3 thousand, rounded upward to 20 thousand because population growth and the trend series remain positive. An 80% interval of roughly +/-55 thousand gives -35 to +75 thousand."},{"kind":"text","text":"Counter-consideration: April's unemployment-rate rise to 4.5% and the ABS note that May has two incoming rotation groups raise downside and survey-volatility risk, so I keep a wide interval that includes another negative employment change."},{"kind":"forecast","point":20,"ciLow":-35,"ciHigh":75}]}
