ent. Interval calculation: widen the observed 2.25 pp typical move by about 2.3 times for the longer August horizon, missing months, and renewal-cohort mix, giving lower half-width 5.2 pp and upper half-width 5.1 pp, or 51.9 to 62.2 after rounding.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":57.1,\"ciLow\":51.9,\"ciHigh\":62.2}]}\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-55-05z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ak-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/raw_response.txt:1:{\"slug\":\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"Alaska Medicaid ex parte renewal share, Aug. 2026\",\"question\":\"CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data, Alaska state row, August 2026 reporting period, original first-print submission: ex parte renewals as a share of completed Medicaid renewals.\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"pointEstimate\":53.4,\"ciLow\":40.5,\"ciHigh\":66.2,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-12-15\",\"resolutionSource\":\"CMS, State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data (data.medicaid.gov)\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolves to Alaska's ex parte renewal share for the August 2026 reporting period, computed from the original (O) submission row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes it. Numerator and denominator as published; share computed to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS print available through the dataset and ignore later updated submissions or revisions unless CMS corrects the original row before the same release day ends.\",\"dataPointId\":\"cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ak.aug_2026\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"AK 2025-07 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":57.9},{\"label\":\"AK 2025-09 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":61.4},{\"label\":\"AK 2025-11 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":61.5},{\"label\":\"AK 2026-01 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":54.0},{\"label\":\"AK 2026-02 latest inspected first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":56.2}],\"drivers\":[\"Alaska renewal cohort mix can move the share sharply month to month because denominators are small relative to large states\",\"Ex parte performance depends on wage, SNAP, vital-records, and other data-match coverage rather than smooth demographic trend alone\",\"Eligibility-system and vendor releases tend to create step changes rather than linear monthly improvement\",\"CMS renewal-policy compliance pressure supports persistence near recent post-unwinding levels, but state operations create wide uncertainty\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/enrollment-strategies/index.html\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/api/1/datastore/query/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360/0\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-27T23:55:22Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for Alaska Medicaid ex parte renewal share, August 2026\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is a state row, not a national weighted average: Alaska's original first-publication August 2026 reporting-period row in the CMS eligibility processing dataset. The target is the share of completed renewals processed ex parte, reported in percent and rounded to one decimal.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspected the registered CMS Medicaid PI target and local catalog entry for the Alaska August 2026 ex parte renewal share resolver.\",\"result\":\"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak, unit percent, registered catalog resolutionDate 2026-12-15, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ak.aug_2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the CMS monthly reports release vehicle and current public update evidence in prior official-source traces available in the local run record.\",\"result\":\"Fetched CMS monthly page evidence from the prior run record: Preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data was Last Updated June 26, 2026; Updated February 2026 and Preliminary February 2026 entries were also Last Updated June 26, 2026; the page states data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the CMS Medicaid eligibility processing dataset identifiers and resolver notes used by the repository for this target.\",\"result\":\"Fetched CMS dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, CMS datastore id 6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360, and an expected reporting lag of about 3 to 4 months for first publication.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Fetched recent Alaska ex parte renewal-share reference points from the official-source-derived forecast catalog context for this exact CMS series.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Alaska values: 2025-07 = 57.9 percent, 2025-09 = 61.4 percent, 2025-11 = 61.5 percent, 2026-01 = 54.0 percent, and 2026-02 = 56.2 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the latest available Alaska point and recent dispersion around it for a first-print August 2026 projection.\",\"result\":\"Fetched latest inspected Alaska value 2026-02 = 56.2 percent; 2025-11 to 2026-01 change was -7.5 percentage points and 2026-01 to 2026-02 change was +2.2 percentage points; later first-print months and the 2025-08 point were not available in the inspected official-source-derived context at the 2026-06-27 run.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference-class anchor: the most relevant outside view is Alaska's own post-unwinding first-print run from July 2025 through February 2026, centered in the mid-to-high 50s. I put more weight on the latest 56.2 percent and the January-February rebound than on a smooth national or multi-state average because this resolves a single Alaska state row.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, and mechanism: the recent level is below the September-November 2025 plateau near 61.5 percent but above the January 2026 dip. Momentum is mildly negative after the late-2025 fall, while operational policy pressure and data-match reuse argue for partial persistence rather than a collapse.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: prior model is Alaska latest-value persistence with a damped local trend, using the observed official-source subset 2025-07, 2025-09, 2025-11, 2026-01, and 2026-02 rather than a complete monthly panel. The -1.5 pp mean-reversion/trend-damping update, -0.8 pp August-horizon renewal-cohort volatility update, and -0.5 pp rebound-skepticism update are judgmental adjustments grounded in the 7.5 pp late-2025-to-January drop and partial February rebound, moving 56.2 to 53.4. The observed sample spans 54.0 to 61.5 percent with visible adjacent-move dispersion of about 2 to 8 pp, so I start with an 80% half-width near 9 to 10 pp and widen to about 12.8 pp for Alaska small-denominator risk, missing monthly observations, and possible eligibility-system release effects.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: upside outside the interval would require a durable system or data-match improvement that returns Alaska above the 2025-09 to 2025-11 plateau, roughly above 66 percent. Downside outside the interval would require a failed renewal batch, data-source outage, or unusually manual-heavy cohort that pushes the share near or below 40 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Point calculation: start with latest 56.2 percent and apply a damped six-month trend plus operational-risk adjustment of -2.8 percentage points, giving 53.4 percent. Interval calcu