e.\",\"result\":\"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar, unit percent, registered resolutionDate 2026-12-15, point 89.8, 80% interval 85.6 to 93.9, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ar.aug_2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the CMS dataset and resolver identifiers attached to the canonical ledger target.\",\"result\":\"Fetched CMS dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, original submission status O, August 2026 reporting period, and one-decimal percent rounding rule for the Arkansas row.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Fetched recent Arkansas ex parte renewal-share reference points from the official-source-derived forecast catalog context for this exact CMS series.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Arkansas values: 2025-07 = 85.9 percent, 2025-09 = 87.1 percent, 2025-11 = 88.8 percent, 2026-01 = 91.1 percent, and 2026-02 = 89.1 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked official-release timing evidence available in the local run context and CMS monthly release vehicle.\",\"result\":\"Fetched ledger resolutionDate 2026-12-15; prior CMS monthly page evidence showed Preliminary March 2026 data Last Updated June 26, 2026 and data.Medicaid.gov monthly update behavior, while no separate future CMS placeholder for the exact August 2026 Arkansas row was exposed in the checked context.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference-class anchor: the most relevant outside view is Arkansas's own recent first-print run for this CMS eligibility-processing series. The five-point sample from July 2025 to February 2026 ranges from 85.9 to 91.1 percent and has a simple average of 88.4 percent, with the latest two observations at 91.1 and 89.1 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, and mechanism: the level is already near the upper end of normal administrative performance, so the forecast should not extrapolate mechanically toward 100. The 2026-02 value of 89.1 is below January's 91.1 but above the 2025 values, consistent with a high plateau plus renewal-cohort noise.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: prior model is Arkansas latest-value persistence with a damped local trend, using five observed first-print values from 2025-07, 2025-09, 2025-11, 2026-01, and 2026-02. The five-point sample center is 88.4 percent and the range is 85.9 to 91.1 percent; I put most weight on latest-value persistence at 89.1, add +0.5 pp for the higher 2026 level versus 2025 and +0.2 pp for mild compliance/operations pressure, yielding 89.8. The 80% interval starts from the 5.2 pp observed sample range, adds about 2.5 pp total for missing-month and cohort-mix uncertainty, and allows a somewhat wider upper tail because automated data matching could improve without hitting the 100 percent ceiling.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: upside outside the interval would require Arkansas to print above 93.9 percent through more complete automated data matching or a renewal cohort unusually suited to ex parte processing. Downside outside the interval would require a manual-heavy renewal cohort, data-source outage, eligibility-system issue, or reporting break pushing the share below 85.6 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Point calculation: latest 89.1 percent plus +0.5 pp damped high-2026-level adjustment plus +0.2 pp mild policy/operations adjustment gives 89.8 percent. Interval calculation: center 89.8, lower half-width 4.2 pp and upper half-width 4.1 pp, reflecting the 5.2 pp recent realized range plus roughly 2.5 pp added uncertainty spread across tails and slight ceiling compression, yielding 85.6 to 93.9 after rounding.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resolution-date note: the canonical ledger target uses 2026-12-15. The checked CMS release context supports the official data.Medicaid.gov monthly release vehicle but did not expose a separate future dated August 2026 Arkansas placeholder, so I keep the forecast tied to the ledger target and bind resolution to the first official CMS dataset print.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Review disposition: accepted the resolver fix by removing the release-day correction exception, made the interval construction more explicit, split the +0.7 pp update into persistence-dominant components, and added the five-point sample size, center, and range. Kept the canonical 2026-12-15 resolutionDate because no exact future CMS placeholder was found in the checked context.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":89.8,\"ciLow\":85.6,\"ciHigh\":93.9}]}\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-55-05z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ak-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/prompt.md:11:- series: cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ak.aug_2026\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-55-05z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ak-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/prompt.md:17:- catalogSlug: \"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\"\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-55-05z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ak-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/prompt.md:19:- dataPointId: \"cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ak.aug_2026\"\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-55-05z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ak-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/prompt.md:22:- resolutionRule: \"Resolves to Alaska's ex parte renewal share for the August 2026 reporting period, computed from the original (O) submission row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes it (expected roughly three to four months after the period). Numerator and denominator as published; share computed to one decimal.\"\n./records/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-57-39z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-al-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/draft_codex_stdout.jsonl:4:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"i